Context. This page belongs to Grothendieck's 1986 'third version' of an axiomatic analysis situs. That project is his attempt to axiomatize 'tame' (modérée) topology in purely combinatorial or order-theoretic terms, through 'ateliers' (workshops) and 'structures spécieuses / polyédrales'. The basic datum is a set M of 'pieces' (open-like subobjects) with:
- a partial order ≤ (inclusion);
- a relation << (written Z <° X: 'well inside', relatively-compact or interior inclusion);
- a symmetric separation relation || (disjointness / non-contact);
- an intersection operation L = X ∩ Y, defined via the associated sets (tilde L = tilde X ∩ tilde Y). The intersection may be empty or may fall outside M.

In an earlier part of the notes the axioms were formulated relative to a distinguished sub-family L (by p.46, the case Λ = L is 'already treated'; the notes' L is distinct from the intersection L = X ∩ Y above). Here Grothendieck takes an arbitrary subfamily Λ ⊂ M, stable under ≤, and relativizes the axioms to Λ.

Key notions:
- omb_Λ(X), the 'shadow' of X in Λ: roughly the elements of Λ well inside / below X. Omb denotes a larger version.
- X'_L := tilde X' ∩ Omb(L), defined on p.44: the part of X' near the intersection L.

The axioms:
- AtΛ1 (density): for every X in M, omb_Λ(X)° ≠ ∅, i.e. there is Z in Λ with Z <° X.
- AtΛ2: X || Y iff X' || Y' for all X' in omb_Λ(X) and Y' in omb_Λ(Y). So separation is detected on Λ-approximations. Λ1 together with Λ2 is called 'Λ très dense'.
- AtΛ3 = AtDΛ (locality of separation): with L = X ∩ Y, X' in omb_Λ(X), Y' in omb_Λ(Y), if X'_L || Y'_L then X' || Y'. Separation of Λ-approximations is decided in a neighbourhood of the intersection. For Λ = L it reduces to the earlier AtL3.
- AtCΛ(spec): a positional relation between X and Y holds iff, for all Λ-approximations X', Y', the condition X'_L = Y'_L = ∅ implies X' || Y'. The symbol is written as X with a crossed comparison sign, apparently 'X and Y are in good / compatible position'. Approximations that miss the intersection region are separated.
- AtCΛ(pol): the same, plus L = ∅ or L ∈ M. In the 'polyhedral' variant, intersections stay in the class.

The implication diagram (dropping 'At'; CΛ* stands for either variant, C* for AtC(spec) or AtC(pol), consistently):
- Λ3 + CΛ* ⇒ C;
- C ⇒ D (vertical arrow);
- Λ2 + Λ3 ⇒ D ⇒ Λ3;
- Λ2 + Λ3 ⇒ Λ2 and D ⇒ D_0;
- D_0 + Λ1 + CΛ* ⇒ Λ2 ⇒ D_0;
- Λ2 + CΛ* ⇔ Λ2 + C*.

Purpose. The next page uses this to give several equivalent complete axiom systems: {Λ1, Λ2, Λ3, CΛ*}, {Λ1, Λ2, D, C*}, {Λ1, CΛ*, D}, {Λ1, Λ2, C*, D_0}. Its upshot is that 'Λ-spécieux' is the same as 'spécieux' (M-spécieux) plus 'Λ très dense'. Thus a tame-topological structure can be presented and checked on any very dense sub-basis Λ: a basis-independence or 'coherence on a dense subfamily' result for this order-theoretic axiomatization.
